yloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"f640bf1595d88852b7bfd0cde6d316993dfd797ac81993fc44d239bfa5a03428","event_uuid":"d0a86e8a-44fa-425b-8bc6-1605054298af","position":{"commit_sha":"4d44a2848ed48575dc7d5862c62d343726036580","position":"1787417621892539001-d0a86e8a-44fa-425b-8bc6-1605054298af"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"b155c906f73c65f2400e529b1f0d840f901d9b0024a3179ebac2b563fa612dec","event_uuid":"5fa65bbf-f76b-496d-bf8b-43deba3a29bd","position":{"commit_sha":"f114f7d61259d73e3208a8e96abb2de1a2c4b80f","position":"1787417982599040366-5fa65bbf-f76b-496d-bf8b-43deba3a29bd"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"UPGRADE: latent risk -> actively failing live eval. Post-merge Live External Integration run 32575679530 (bedrock, job 97037577692): the re-denominated 0707 eval fails 0/3 with responses_at_bank=[6,7,8,9,9] (3/3 identical, temp 0) — the model's first GENUINE bank lands at evidence response 6 against the 3-response bound, while the policy's silent per-criterion fallbacks fire on schedule (source=\"fallback\", invisible to the eval's deliberate source==\"tool\" observer). System-level boundedness holds; model-driven interleaved records no longer happen without the removed COMMIT_STEERING_NOTICE pressure. This ticket now decides the fork stated in the description — adopt an in-band commit-due nudge (eval turns green as-is) or accept/rescope (the eval's oracle must then count fallback banks, a contract re-scope). It blocks 9507-4676-27af-4344's final acceptance criterion; evidence and stub replay details are in the RCA trail there.","timestamp":1787410989150807001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"OPERATOR RULING (2026-08-22): option (b) approved — re-scope the 0707 dense-banking eval to system-level boundedness. The oracle counts durable banking events regardless of actor (genuine model bank_progress calls AND the policy's fallback snapshots), asserting progress is durably banked at bounded intervals. No steering nudge is added; the model's voluntary banking cadence is no longer the measured contract. Rationale: post-dd41 the fallback snapshots are the durability mechanism; an eval red on model etiquette while the system is safe is noise.","timestamp":1787416698626834001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implementation validated locally per the operator ruling (system-level boundedness):\n\n- Observer re-scoped: tests/_bank_observer.py make_observed_upsert now records the FIRST durable bank write of each criterion regardless of actor (genuine model record OR policy bounded-fallback insufficiency snapshot); only seeded=True cache seeds are excluded. bounded_bank_gaps assertion unchanged (max_gap=3 evidence responses).\n- Eval + shared docstrings name the ruled contract (this ticket) and the run-32575679530 evidence.\n- Unit regressions (tests/unit/test_completion_banking_oracle.py, real CompletionEvidencePolicy driven by a stubbed toolset):\n  * fallback-only transcript GREEN: model never records; fallbacks bank all 5 at snapshots [2,5,8,11,14], gaps <=3.\n  * live-shape GREEN: fallbacks at [2,5] + genuine records at [6,7,8] -> [2,5,6,7,8] (the 32575679530 signature under system scope).\n  * genuinely-unbounded RED in FINAL oracle form: _Rig(fallback_banks=False) -> responses_at_bank [6,6,6,6,6], oracle rejects (strict test-modification order satisfied).\n  * Mutation checks: (A) dropping the gap bound -> unbounded test fails; (B) reverting the observer to the source=='tool' filter -> actor-agnostic forwarding test fails. Both restored; final form 10/10 green.\n- Gates: make lint, make typecheck (mypy 636 files clean), complexity ratchet new=0 increased=0.\n\nVALIDATION LIMIT: the live bedrock arm cannot run locally. Stub replay against the real policy proves the oracle semantics on the proven [2,5,8,...] snapshot schedule; live confirmation lands on the next scheduled/dispatched external-integration run.","timestamp":1787417621892539001}],"created_at":1787405164851895001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"d88d6076-5708-43a8-b958-22d583df97c3","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"9507-4676-27af-4344"},{"link_uuid":"48608cdf-4837-407c-8d37-6c08acbe668e","relation":"blocks","target_id":"9507-4676-27af-4344"},{"link_uuid":"5fa65bbf-f76b-496d-bf8b-43deba3a29bd","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"22a7-c5c6-ecfa-4bbd"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nOperator ruling (recorded in comments, 2026-08-22): option (b) approved. The 0707 dense-banking\neval (`tests/external/test_completion_banking_behavior_0707.py`) is re-scoped to SYSTEM-level\nboundedness: the oracle counts durable banking events regardless of actor — genuine model\n`record_criterion_verdict` upserts AND the policy's silent bounded-fallback insufficiency\nsnapshots — and asserts progress is durably banked at bounded evidence-response intervals. No\nsteering nudge is added to production; the model's voluntary banking cadence is explicitly no\nlonger the measured contract.\n\nWhy: commit e1352535ace (ticket dd41-239d-6e09-4a86) deliberately let batched governed evidence\nreads execute and removed the COMMIT_STEERING_NOTICE pressure that had made the model interleave\ngenuine records. Post-merge run 32575679530 proved the system bound still holds (the policy's\nper-criterion 3-response fallbacks fire on schedule, source=\"fallback\", snapshots one response\nlow per the documented ordering caveat: 2/5/8), but the eval's observer counts only\nsource==\"tool\" writes, so the model's genuine first banks at responses [6,7,8,9,9] fail the\n3-response bound 3/3 deterministically. The observer's actor filter is the last stale facet of\nthe pre-dd41 contract.\n\n## Approach\n\nTest-only change; no production code. In the shared seam `tests/_bank_observer.py`, re-scope\n`make_observed_upsert`'s bookkeeping from `source == \"tool\"` to any durable run-time bank write\nregardless of source, EXCLUDING cache seeds (`seeded=True` marks pre-run cache seeding, not run\nprogress). Keep the bounded-gap oracle (`bounded_bank_gaps`) unchanged — it already bounds\nfirst-bank gaps in evidence responses. Update the module docstring, the eval's docstring, and\nthe oracle regression's docstring to name the ruled contract (system-level boundedness,\noperator ruling on this ticket). Update the unit regressions:\n\n- `tests/unit/test_completion_bank_observer_forwarding.py`: the first-write bookkeeping test now\n  asserts a fallback-sourced write IS recorded and a seeded write is NOT.\n- `tests/unit/test_completion_banking_oracle.py`: add a GREEN case proving a fallback-only\n  transcript (model never records; the REAL policy fail-closes every criterion at its\n  per-criterion 3-response boundary, observed snapshots [2,5,8,11,14]) passes the oracle; add a\n  RED case proving the oracle in final form REJECTS a genuinely-unbounded system (fallback\n  disabled via a no-op fallback_record, model banks only after 6 evidence responses →\n  first gap > 3); add a replay of the live run-32575679530 shape (silent fallbacks + genuine\n  records from response 6) proving it is GREEN under the ruled scope.\n\nValidation limit: the live bedrock arm cannot run locally. Local validation is the stub replay\nthrough the REAL `wrap_completion_evidence_policy` (the proven [2/5/8] fallback snapshot\nschedule gives gaps within bound 3). Live confirmation lands on the next scheduled/dispatched\nexternal-integration run.\n\n## Scope\n\n- tests/_bank_observer.py\n- tests/external/test_completion_banking_behavior_0707.py\n- tests/unit/test_completion_banking_oracle.py\n- tests/unit/test_completion_bank_observer_forwarding.py\n\n## Testing\n\n`python -m pytest tests/unit/test_completion_banking_oracle.py tests/unit/test_completion_bank_observer_forwarding.py -q`\nin the worktree venv; external module collects cleanly. Strict test-modification order: the\nrevised oracle+observer are seen RED in final form against a genuinely-unbounded transcript\n(no-op fallback, late model banks) before the change counts; mutation check re-runs the GREEN\nfallback-only case with the gap bound dropped to confirm teeth.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `make_observed_upsert` records the first durable bank write of each criterion regardless\n  of `source`, excluding `seeded=True` cache seeds, verified by the updated forwarding\n  regression.\n- [ ] A fallback-only transcript through the REAL policy (snapshots [2,5,8,11,14]) PASSES the\n  oracle, and the live run-32575679530 shape (fallbacks at 2/5 + genuine records from response\n  6) PASSES, each asserted by a dedicated unit case.\n- [ ] A genuinely-unbounded transcript (fallback disabled, first durable bank after >3 evidence\n  responses) FAILS the oracle, asserted by a dedicated unit case run in the final oracle form.\n- [ ] Docstrings in the shared seam, the eval, and the oracle regression name the ruled\n  system-level contract and cite this ticket's operator ruling.\n- [ ] No files outside the four declared test paths change; `make lint`, `make typecheck`, and\n  `python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check` pass in the worktree venv.\n- [ ] The validation limit (live bedrock unavailable locally; next external-integration run is\n  the live confirmation) is stated in a ticket comment at close.\n","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"tests/_bank_observer.py","reason":"re-scope observed_upsert bookkeeping to actor-agnostic durable bank writes"},{"path":"tests/external/test_completion_banking_behavior_0707.py","reason":"docstring names the ruled system-level contract"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_completion_banking_oracle.py","reason":"GREEN fallback-only + live-shape cases; RED genuinely-unbounded case"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_completion_bank_observer_forwarding.py","reason":"first-write bookkeeping asserts fallback counted, seeded excluded"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["blocks","9507-4676-27af-4344"],["relates_to","22a7-c5c6-ecfa-4bbd"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"c7266cb2-0480-42b3-97d9-1f310e5331a1","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"6543-24a7-d2fb-4ff9","ticket_type":"task","title":"Decide whether batched evidence responses need a commit-due nudge","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["a7c156bf-717f-4457-88ec-a4e80b7950f6","d88d6076-5708-43a8-b958-22d583df97c3","256f6d1b-be8b-4807-bd59-353c7eaa161c","48608cdf-4837-407c-8d37-6c08acbe668e","0c695b71-8cb5-4c3d-880a-dd66f4ab8e0c","de2174e2-a0e9-462c-a2e2-34a7c09f89c4","fec0bee7-8daf-4337-8e31-33d2586ec7f9","37cc3fc7-ce82-4169-8ebb-6798c82fcf0c","c7266cb2-0480-42b3-97d9-1f310e5331a1","7f32b6bb-ef0e-4ef9-a901-192673c53c4b","d0a86e8a-44fa-425b-8bc6-1605054298af","5fa65bbf-f76b-496d-bf8b-43deba3a29bd"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787421917765578614,"uuid":"53e15467-7246-45b6-afba-9857ba09c566"}